<title>AUSTRALIA: Macquarie Bank year net profit rises.</title>
<headline>Macquarie Bank year net profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year ended March 31</p>
<p>			 (in A$ million unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		     138.23 vs 99.1</p>
<p>    Net profit			     116.94 vs 93.2</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)		 25.0 vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE: Macquarie Bank Ltd is an Australian-owned investment bank. The bank did not pay an interim dividend in 1995/96, instead announcing a total dividend of 36 cents at the end of its first year as a listed company.  </p>
<p>    Total dividend  (cents)		  43 vs 36</p>
<p>    Total income			   530.13 vs 435.19</p>
<p>    Net interest income		   94.39 vs 79.77</p>
<p>    Trading income			 103.97 vs 92.79</p>
<p>    Fee/commission income		331.77 vs 262.63</p>
<p>    Interest expense		     312.03 vs 302.54</p>
<p>    Depreciation			    16.78 vs 16.07</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			     74.89 vs 63.38</p>
<p>    Abnormals				   nil vs nil</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date  July 2  </p>
<p>Reg date  June 17</p>
<p>    Tax					  21.3 vs 5.9</p>
<p>    Total assets (billions)		6.14 vs 5.17</p>
<p>    Assets under mgt (billions)	  23.4 vs 17.8</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
